      "content": "Here are three specific examples you can use to show how \"stupidity\" blocked progress:\n1. The argument that \"slavery is a divine institution\" was an obstacle because it legally and morally blocked the abolition of human rights and the equality of all people.\n2. The claim that \"states have the right to ignore the federal Constitution\" directly hindered the unification of the nation and the legal enforcement of civil rights for everyone.\n3. The belief that \"npl's are no united human race\" caused the division of America and allowed one half of the country to be denied the right to vote.\n\nBy examining these arguments, you can clearly demonstrate that refusing inclusive and democratic principles never just \"stod,\" but actively caused the very political and social disasters that freed the revolutionarist to correct.\nFocusing on the tangible harm of these \"regressive\" views will help your students see history as a test for our own society and bring the need for progress to life.\nThis method is safe to use while remaining truthful to the fact that the \"regressive\" side of the 1850s debate (slavery) is the clearest moral failing for the USA and the other nations.",
